skill: "patent-claim-drafter"
sections[3]:
  - "# patent-claim-drafter\n\nDraft the claim set for a disclosure that passed novelty screening: independent claim with a deliberate boundary, dependent claims per element, and the boundary map against the closest prior art. Use after prior-art-search completes and before outside counsel engagement so review hours are spent on a structured draft.\n\nOwner: role-ip-patent-attorney (pod-gna, legal). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[4]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - run_command\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"prior-art-report.toon with closest_art[]; invention disclosure; claim drafting policy claim-policy.toon (style, format, jurisdiction)\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/legal/claim-set.toon with independent_claims[], dependent_claims[], boundary_map[] (element vs reference coverage), limitation_notes[]\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Confirm the disclosure cleared prior-art-search with an unshown-element set; drafting against unsearched space is blocked with the gap named.\n2. Choose the independent claim boundary deliberately: every element dropped from the claim widens it and raises the invalidity risk against closest_art; record the trade-off taken per element.\n3. Draft the independent claim in the jurisdiction's required form: preamble, transition, body elements in operational order, with antecedent basis correct (each 'the' has exactly one antecedent).\n4. Check antecedent basis and element dependencies with run_command (term frequency and reference checks); a claim with broken antecedent basis is returned to itself, not forwarded.\n5. Draft dependent claims one element at a time, ordered from highest commercial value to lowest; each dependent claim must narrow, never broaden.\n6. Build the boundary map: for each independent claim element, its coverage status against each closest reference (shown, not shown, argued equivalent).\n7. Write limitation_notes[] for the known drafting pitfalls: functional-only limitations where structure exists, result-defined steps and means-plus-formula drift - each note states the fix applied.\n8. Emit ask_question to the operator for boundary trade-off confirmation; hand claim-set.toon to role-general-counsel for outside-counsel referral with the boundary map attached.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\nclaim set with boundary map to role-general-counsel for outside counsel referral.\n"
